WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.780
Hi Justin and Laura. How are you?

2
00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:04.930
Good.
So good.

3
00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:06.673
So happy to be here. Hi, Laura.

4
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.433
Hey.

5
00:00:08.433 --> 00:00:11.340
I love that you are bringing this story out there.

6
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:15.530
I know that Zach went viral with his song,

7
00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:19.820
but that's different than telling the story

8
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:24.433
behind the song, and about the person, and about the life.

9
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:29.140
You know, Laura, when Justin approached you,

10
00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:30.860
what did you think at that time?

11
00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:34.750
Well, when Justin approached us, it had already,

12
00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:37.540 line:15%
the story had already kind of been out there.

13
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.620 line:15%
We'd already had, I think CNN had been to our house.

14
00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.530 line:15%
And so there was a lot of stir.

15
00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:46.920
And so actually his reaching out to us

16
00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.670
kind of got buried in all of it.

17
00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:51.790
And he got to us in a unique way.

18
00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:54.657
He knew that Zach really loved Rainn Wilson,

19
00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:59.200
from "The Office", his character Dwight.

20
00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:02.270
And so he had Rainn reach out to Zach.

21
00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:04.864
And that's actually how we got connected with Justin.

22
00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.092
(Justin laughing)

23
00:01:07.092 --> 00:01:09.340
(laughing) Which was great.It was perfect.

24
00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:10.740
I love that.

25
00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:11.882
Yeah.

26
00:01:11.882 --> 00:01:16.093
And, you know, I heard that you promised Zach

27
00:01:16.093 --> 00:01:19.963
that you would do whatever you could to tell his story.

28
00:01:19.963 --> 00:01:24.963
And how did that sort of conversation start, may I ask?

29
00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:32.824
Zach was one of these rare kids that just had this wisdom.

30
00:01:32.824 --> 00:01:35.830
And I just remember feeling in awe of who he was.

31
00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:39.530 line:15%
And being like, 10 years older, I wanted to be like him.

32
00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:42.730 line:15%
You know, he just, he changed my world, my perspective.

33
00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:44.210 line:15%
And so before he died,

34
00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:46.320
I remember being on FaceTime with him.

35
00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.270
And I just, I told him, I made him a promise.

36
00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:51.560
I said, "Bro, I'm gonna not stop

37
00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:54.460
until we make sure your story is seen and heard

38
00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:55.293
all over the world."

39
00:01:55.293 --> 00:01:57.330
And more than that, also, that we would raise money

40
00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:58.400
for his fund.

41
00:01:58.400 --> 00:01:59.233 line:15%
Before he died,

42
00:01:59.233 --> 00:02:01.240 line:15%
he set up the Zach Sobiech Osteosarcoma Fund,

43
00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:03.650 line:15%
and that was a part of my promise.

44
00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:06.990 line:15%
And of course the week, like the day of his funeral,

45
00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:08.680 line:15%
after the documentary first went viral

46
00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.710
he hit number one on iTunes.

47
00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:14.580
And three days after the movie came out this year,

48
00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:15.930
he hit number one again.

49
00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:18.860
He became the first unsigned artist to hit number one twice.

50
00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:21.130
And the best thing is all that money goes

51
00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:24.611
to his fund to help cure cancer.

52
00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:25.711
(audience applauding)

53
00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:28.800
May I ask Justin, what was the impetus for you

54
00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:29.633
to reach out?

55
00:02:29.633 --> 00:02:32.080
Because that's an incredible endeavor to spend years

56
00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:35.070
of your life invested in this friendship

57
00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:37.510
and telling the story and honoring.

58
00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:41.400
Was there a catalyst, something personal for you

59
00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.510
that made you connect with Zach, even from afar?

60
00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:46.730
This whole thing started because I just,

61
00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:50.280 line:15%
I believe that every human being on this planet

62
00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:54.750 line:15%
has an opportunity to be of service with their talents.

63
00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:58.530 line:15%
And I wanted to have conversations that challenged us,

64
00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:02.090
to maybe start to think about our mortality in a good way.

65
00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:03.460
Like maybe it can be an ally

66
00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:04.890
and it can influence the way we live.

67
00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:07.510
And so that's why I started with this documentary series.

68
00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:09.470
And subsequently have just been trying to figure out,

69
00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:13.400
how with my unique gifts, can I just help people

70
00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.070
see the beauty that is life.

71
00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:16.980
That we're freakin' alive.

72
00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:19.200
So, when I found Zach, when I met Zack,

73
00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.261
when I got to know Laura, who is a living, breathing saint.

74
00:03:23.261 --> 00:03:24.850
Although she would disagree,

75
00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.870
because she loves talking about her imperfections.

76
00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:29.680
I just felt like this was a unique story

77
00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.950
and mixed with music, that could impact

78
00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:33.930
and touch millions of lives.

79
00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:36.200
And Laura, you wrote a book.

80
00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.843
It seems so obvious, like such an obvious question,

81
00:03:38.843 --> 00:03:40.941
why did you want to write this book?

82
00:03:40.941 --> 00:03:43.770
But, how did you write this book?

83
00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:47.710
What I really wanted to do is show our family life

84
00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:49.470 line:15%
under the hood a little bit, you know?

85
00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:52.513 line:15%
Just like, okay, you've been inspired by this person.

86
00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:57.750 line:15%
Here's how we did it. We did it imperfectly.

87
00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:00.750
We were clunky at times. We fought at times.

88
00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:04.540
We cried, we argued, we wrestled through this.

89
00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:06.360
And I really wanted people to see that

90
00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:08.440
because I knew the tendency was to kind of look

91
00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:11.210
at our family and think that we had it all together.

92
00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:12.540
And we didn't.

93
00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:16.500
And I think that's really the beauty of the story is.

94
00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:20.340
That's where people can say "Oh, I'm like that.

95
00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:22.790
And if I'm like that, then maybe I can do this too."

96
00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:27.790
And so I think too often we allow our own insecurities

97
00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:31.210
and, you know, what other people might think,

98
00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:33.310
or the fact that we're not perfect people.

99
00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:37.320
We let those things stop us from doing big things.

100
00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:40.392
And I think that's one of the lessons Zack taught me.

101
00:04:40.392 --> 00:04:41.225
(audience applauding)

102
00:04:41.225 --> 00:04:43.810
I'm in awe of everything that you guys are doing.

103
00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:48.690
And I just appreciate everything that you have done

104
00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:50.320
and upheld with Zach's life.

105
00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.613
And now continue to share it with us

106
00:04:52.613 --> 00:04:55.603
through this beautiful movie "Clouds".

107
00:04:55.603 --> 00:04:56.436
(audience applauding)

108
00:04:56.436 --> 00:04:57.860
So thank you for coming.

109
00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:59.560
Thank you for being so kind.

110
00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:00.393
It's such an example

111
00:05:00.393 --> 00:05:02.410
of like the goodness exists in our business.

112
00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:04.110
I'm just, I'm grateful for you.

113
00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:05.610
Thanks for saying that, Justin.

114
00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.040
Literally, I'm like looking at you.

115
00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:10.210
I'm like Justin, you're a saint. You're so rad.

116
00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:11.350
How did like...
Oh no.

117
00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:13.170
This is so awesome.

118
00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:14.600
You know, you are a really good person

119
00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:16.000
and this is really important.

120
00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:19.880
And Laura, for you to be so strong and

121
00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:22.530
be talking about the human experience

122
00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:23.620
in the way that you do

123
00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:25.590
with everything that you've been through.

124
00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:28.870
And continue to uphold, is just mind blowing.

125
00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:32.577
Really. I'm very honored to speak with you both today.

126
00:05:32.577 --> 00:05:36.300
"Clouds" is available now on Disney+.

127
00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:38.090
Thank you Justin and Laura,
Thank you so much.

128
00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:40.093
for bringing me into your conversation.

129
00:05:40.093 --> 00:05:41.720
(audience applauding)

130
00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:43.360
Thank you.
Love you, Laura.

131
00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:44.610
Love you too.

